ght by  Bucky Bailey whose mother worked at that  DuPont plant in Parkersburg West  Virginia and was born with severe birth  defects Bucky was also portrayed in the  movie dark waters so Bucky thank you for  being here when we first met you for our  report on twenty twenty years ago you  were just getting married and concerned  that given the high levels of the  chemical in your blood any children you  might have had would have suffered the  same plight  so Bucky bring us up to date well it  took us several years to get to a point  where we wanted to have children just  due to the struggles that I faced in my  life  genetics told us that uh my children  would have a 50% chance of contracting  the same birth deformities so it took us  quite a few years to get to a point  where we did finally through prayer and  faith we made the choice and I now have  two beautiful children three-year-old  son and a two month old daughter and  they are the love of my life and I'm  supremely blessed that's great news a  question now from our control room and  executive producer Rhonda Schwarz Rhonda  so Rob you were able to get an  astonishing DuPont settled with you for  six hundred fifty million dollars if you  had thirty five hundred clients but what  about Bucky Bailey's Bar in there you  know unfortunately the scope of the  study that was done you know we set up  this massive human health study to try  to have independent scientists look at  all of the data including what was in  DuPont's internal files including their  own study which showed that two out of  the seven women at the DuPont plant had  children with these defects including  unfortunately Bucky as we all know and  that the panel we put together an  independent panel to look at all that  data try to do a bigger study so that  they could get enough cases and enough  instances to be able to confirm which  diseases were linked they were able to  link six different diseases including  two types of cancer but  fortunately 